  "metadata": {
    "title": "Toxicity and hallucination are different risks",
    "description": "Toxicity is harmful generated text measured by classifiers over many continuations. Hallucination can conflict with real-world facts (factuality) or with the provided input (faithfulness). FActScore checks atomic claims against sources; grounding and abstention reduce risk but do not eliminate it."
